<BaseLayout title="Affiliate Disclosure — Where Is Baldo?" description="Affiliate Disclosure for whereisbaldo.com">
  <div class="post-header">
    <span class="post-tag">Legal</span>
    <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    <p class="post-meta">Effective Date: May 2026 · whereisbaldo.com</p>
  </div>
  <div class="post-body legal-body">

    <h2>The Short Version</h2>
    <p>Some links on this blog are affiliate links. If you click one and buy something, I may earn a small commission — at no extra cost to you. This helps keep the blog running so I can keep traveling and writing.</p>

    <h2>What That Actually Means</h2>
    <p>whereisbaldo.com participates in affiliate marketing programs. This means that when I recommend a product, service, hotel, or experience and include a link, that link may be a tracked affiliate link. If you make a purchase through that link, I receive a small percentage of the sale as compensation from the company — not from you.</p>
    <p>The price you pay is exactly the same whether you use my link or go directly to the site.</p>

    <h2>My Promise to You</h2>
    <p>I only recommend things I genuinely believe in or have personally used. Affiliate relationships do not influence which destinations I cover, what I say about a place, or whether my review is positive or negative. If something was bad, I'll say it was bad.</p>
    <p>My opinions are my own. Always.</p>

    <h2>FTC Compliance</h2>
    <p>In accordance with the U.S. Federal Trade Commission (FTC) guidelines, I disclose that this blog may receive compensation through affiliate links. This disclosure applies site-wide — any link on whereisbaldo.com could potentially be an affiliate link.</p>
    <p>Posts that contain affiliate links will typically be noted within the post itself.</p>

    <h2>Current Affiliate Programs</h2>
    <p>This blog may participate in programs including but not limited to: Amazon Associates, Booking.com Affiliate Program, Hotels.com, GetYourGuide, travel insurance partners, and other travel-related services. This list may change as the blog grows.</p>

    <h2>Questions?</h2>
    <p>If you're ever unsure whether a link is an affiliate link, or if you have questions about this policy, reach out at <strong><a href="mailto:baldolanded@gmail.com">baldolanded@gmail.com</a></strong></p>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-body h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
